MPI is a standard that provides an interface that allows parallel applications to run. It specifies which functions are called, how arguments passed to them are used and what the response should be when the function is executed. It allows data interchange between the memory of nodes in a computer network or high-quality multicore computer. It is used to write parallelized programs by dividing the database into small portions or tasks that can run simultaneously.

