Gradient checkpointing does reduce memory usage when compared to backpropagation by only storing the identity/input for a selected layer while computing the gradients for that layer. However, to better understand gradient checkpointing, let's first go through the vanilla backward pass using backpropagation. The memory utilization during a backward pass without gradient checkpointing is explained in the following diagram:

![No gradient checkpointing, backpropagation](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1055534731775584286/1074977556701634570/memory_utilization_backprop.png)

As you can see, all intermediate outputs of each layer are stored in memory during the backward pass to compute gradients. When the model is deep or wide, it might require more memory than your device has available.

Now let's look at the mechanism of gradient checkpointing. The main idea is recomputing the intermediate outputs instead of storing them in memory when needed during the backward pass.

![Gradient checkpointing](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1055534731775584286/1074978406642751539/gradient_checkpointing_high_level.png)

The memory utilization during the backward pass using gradient checkpointing:

![Gradient checkpointing, memory utilization](https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1055534731775584286/1074979130640240650/memory_utilization_checkpointing.png)

In [PyTorch](https://pytorch.org/), gradient checkpointing can be implemented using the `torch.utils.checkpoint` function. This will automatically handle the forward pass, checkpoint some layers, and perform recomputation during the backward pass. Here's an example of checkpointing in PyTorch:

```python
import torch
import torch.nn as nn
import torch.nn.functional as F

def checkpoint_layer(layer):
    def forward_checkpointed(input):
        def save(x):
            return x
        def load(x):
            return x
        return torch.utils.checkpoint(lambda x: layer(x),
                                       input, save, load)
    return forward_checkpointed

class ResNet18_checkpoint(nn.Module):
