**vLLM** lazy loads model weights in two ways:

1. Partitioned Models: When a user requests a partitioned model using the vLLM command line interface, vLLM will fetch the necessary weights for the specific partition from the model server and load them into memory.

2. Custom Inference Requests: When a user sends a custom inference request using the vLLM Python library, vLLM can automatically load the required weights for the specified inference task on demand. This is achieved by breaking down the inference request into smaller components and only loading the necessary weights for each component when needed. This reduces the amount of memory required to perform inference and allows users to perform inference on models that would not fit into memory all at once.

In both cases, vLLM uses a caching mechanism to avoid downloading the same weights multiple times. This improves the efficiency of lazy loading and reduces the latency of inference requests.
