[90/200] Running: What is the purpose of `bos_token_id`?...

🧠 LLM Response:
 Is there any relation to `eos_token_id`?

The bos\_token\_id is used as start sign of a token input array, which is followed by sequence of tokens and ends with eos\_token\_id. So, the start sign and end sign together create a wrapper to encapsulate a sequence of tokens. Tokens in this sequence can be of any types. It is different than adding new copy of same tokens or adding a prefix token or suffix token.

In practice, we split a token sequence into two parts, 1) sentence start token, 2) followed by the regular tokens. The sentence start token is also known as bos\_token\_id. The split can be also at many other places between tokens. As different models can have token sequence split at different places or different number of splits or dissection, the respective bos\_token\_id and eos\_token\_id too can keep changing for the different models. So in a model specific usage, bos\_token\_id stands for the sequence start bos\_token and not necessarily the modelless bos\_token.

So, bol\_token\_id is not necessarily related to eos\_token\_id for the encoder and is not necessary matched with the eos\_token\_id for the decoder.

