-----------------------------------------------

| Key                   | Type                                                  | Value (Example)                                                        |
|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `prompt.prefix`     | string                                                 | "I want to ask a model that takes only text as input and generates a text as output." |
| `prompt.suffix`     | string                                                 | ""                             |
| `prompt.syntax`      | string                                                 | "[text]"                               |
| `prompt.boundary`    | string                                                 | `[ # of chars ]`           |
| `prompt.support`     | JSON Object                                             |{"Version": "v1.0","Platform": "platform.openai.com","Model": "currency","Params": {"precision": 2,"currencySymbol": "$"}} |

---

--------

* `prompt.prefix`: *string* - (Optional): The "leading" string that the model will output a response to. Generally, this value is predefined to an explicit template string which guides the user to interact with the model.
* `prompt.suffix`: *string* - (Optional): The "trailing" string that the model will output a response to. Generally, this value is predefined to an empty string.
* `prompt.syntax`: *string* - (Optional): The syntax of the prompt/request containing a reference to the input data that the ChatML model will process. Input reference delimiter in ChatML is denoted by `[text]` which lets the model knows where exactly to consume the input data.
* `prompt.boundary`: *object* - (Optional): The object that denotes the maximum amount (in characters) consumned by the model in its response.
* `prompt.support`: *JSON Object* - (Optional): The JSON object containing the metadata of the Supported Model (i.e. the model's version, platform, and model type and any associated parameters). This value is specific to each model and must be provided when calling the ChatML service.

--------

--------

**NOTE**: The `prompt` example above is using the OpenAI's `currency` model as a call example, for more information about the `currency` model and [supported models](https://platform.openai.com/docs/models) please check the OpenAI website.

